    {"id": "v03-compartir-cadaqu-s", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 3, "badge": "ELBULLI LINE", "name": "Compartir Cadaqués", "short": "Compartir Cadaqués", "lat": 42.28934, "lng": 3.27602, "productTags": ["Contemporary", "Fish"], "why": "Before Disfrutar in Barcelona, Mateu Casañas, Oriol Castro and Eduard Xatruch, who met in the elBulli kitchen at Cala Montjoi over the hill, opened this room in Cadaqués in 2012. The rule is in the name: nothing arrives as an individual plate, everything goes to the middle. The chef's menu now runs to about ten savoury courses and three sweets. Their Barcelona house later took a third star (November 2023) and the World's 50 Best No.1 (June 2024).", "address": "Riera de Sant Vicenç s/n, 17488 Cadaqués", "phone": "+34 972 258 482", "hours": "Call ahead: no 2026 season dates found. Traded March-May 2026 (dated reviews); Time Out says opening days vary through the year and past records say it closes in deep winter · Call ahead: ma.to lists Tuesday to Saturday; Time Out says days vary through the year", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Compartir+Cadaqués+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "Chef's menu about EUR 80 per person (Macarfi); Time Out range EUR 30-100 (seen Oct 2026)", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "Shared plates from the three chefs behind Disfrutar, in an old stone house on the Cadaqués riverbed.", "verdict": "For a long shared lunch with the whole table on one menu, and the closest the coast gets to the elBulli lineage at a fraction of the Barcelona bill. Go with an open mind on the menu and start with the gazpacho.", "dishes": [{"name": "Chef's sharing menu", "note": "About ten courses and three desserts for the whole table; around EUR 80 (Macarfi)", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Gazpacho with pesto", "note": "The cold starter the house is known for", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Empordà seafood rice", "note": "The rice at the centre of the menu", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Tuna roll", "note": "Named by diners in spring 2026", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Sea bass", "note": "The fish course diners praised in 2026", "kind": "dish"}], "reservation": "Book ahead by phone or online; the menu is served to the whole table", "caveat": "Opening days change through the year and no 2026 closing date was found: phone before an autumn visit. Reviews in March-April 2026 are mixed on the menu's value; service and the courtyard are praised.", "neighborhood": "Cadaqués · Riera de Sant Vicenç", "signal_chip": {"label": "Michelin", "full": "MICHELIN Guide selection, no star · 2 Soles Guía Repsol", "cosign": "the elBulli line on the water"}, "category": "village", "charter": {"price": "Chef's menu about EUR 80 per person (Macarfi); Time Out range EUR 30-100 (seen Oct 2026)", "book": "Book ahead by phone or online; the menu is served to the whole table", "warn": "Opening days change through the year and no 2026 closing date was found: phone before an autumn visit. Reviews in March-April 2026 are mixed on the menu's value; service and the courtyard are praised.", "fit": "Shared plates from the three chefs behind Disfrutar, in an old stone house on the Cadaqués riverbed."}},
    {"id": "v12-espai-del-peix-llotja-de-palam-s", "cat": "market", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 12, "badge": "PRODUCE", "name": "Espai del Peix / Llotja de Palamós", "short": "Espai del Peix / Llotja ", "lat": 41.84454, "lng": 3.12712, "tags": ["Palamós · the fishing quay", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 19 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Fish", "Produce", "Market"], "why": "The Palamós fish market sells its catch by Dutch auction: the price falls on a board until a buyer stops it. The Museu de la Pesca runs half-hour guided visits that explain the bidding live through a large window over the floor, usually at 4.30pm and 5pm; they cost EUR 3.50 in 2025. Next door, the Espai del Peix kitchen teaches what to do with the less famous fish, and cooked at the 11th Fira de la Gamba on 13 June 2026.", "address": "Edifici de la Llotja, Moll Pesquer s/n, 17230 Palamós", "phone": "", "hours": "Year-round on set dates; 2026 activity confirmed (Fira de la Gamba 13 June, show-cooking 21 May). Autumn 2026 visit dates not found · Call ahead: 2024-25 listings show visits at 4.30pm and 5pm on specific weekdays (not daily); the old record said auction Mon-Fri from about 4pm", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Espai+del+Peix+/+Llotja+de+Palamós+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "Auction visit EUR 3.50, free under 4 (seen 2025 listings, Oct 2026); workshops about EUR 20 (older listing)", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "Watch the Palamós catch sold at the falling-price auction, then cook fish with the quay's own kitchen.", "verdict": "The best hour in Palamós for a chef or a curious guest: book the auction visit first, then eat the prawn on the port. Check dates before going, since visits run on set days rather than every weekday.", "dishes": [{"name": "Guided auction visit", "note": "Thirty minutes over the auction floor with the Museu de la Pesca; EUR 3.50 in 2025", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Gamba de Palamós", "note": "Seen graded and sold before it reaches any restaurant", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Show-cooking and tasting", "note": "Espai del Peix cooks working the day's fish", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Saturday cooking workshop", "note": "Hands-on fish cookery for adults; about EUR 20 in an older listing", "kind": "dish"}], "web": "https://www.espaidelpeix.org", "reservation": "Book the auction visit and workshops through the Museu de la Pesca or Espai del Peix", "caveat": "Visits run on announced dates only, and there is no auction at weekends or when the fleet stays in. The 2026 visit price was not found.", "neighborhood": "Palamós · the fishing quay", "signal_chip": {"label": "Live auction", "full": "Working Llotja de Palamós with Museu de la Pesca guided visits · Fira de la Gamba 2026", "cosign": "see the prawn sold before it is cooked"}, "category": "larder", "hot_this_month": "The trawlers are working this autumn, before their winter stop (2 Jan-16 Feb in 2025): watch the weekday afternoon auction now (checked 19 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v13-anxoves-sol-s", "cat": "berth", "tier": "berth_top", "priority": 3, "badge": "PRODUCE", "name": "Anxoves Solés", "short": "Anxoves Solés", "lat": 42.12597, "lng": 3.13366, "tags": ["L'Escala · Closa d'en Llop", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 19 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Produce", "Fish"], "why": "The Solés family has salted anchovies in L'Escala since 1888, and the factory stands in the oldest salting building left in the town. For the company's 130th anniversary it opened a museum inside the working plant, with audio guides in seven languages on how the fish is layered in salt, pressed and filleted by hand. The ticket ends with a tasting on the terrace outside, where the shop sells the jars.", "address": "Carrer Closa d'en Llop 40, 17130 L'Escala", "phone": "", "hours": "Year-round; trading in April 2026 (dated review) · Call ahead: one ticket listing gives about 9am-7pm weekdays and 10am-2pm weekends; no own-site hours found", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Anxoves+Solés+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "Museum and tasting about EUR 6-8 by platform (seen Oct 2026); jars and tins priced individually", "reservation": "Walk-in for the shop; museum tickets online or at the door", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "L'Escala's oldest salting house: anchovies cured on site since 1888, with a museum and a tasting terrace.", "verdict": "The larder stop for anyone provisioning a galley or taking food home. Do the museum and tasting, then buy the fillets in oil and a jar of seitons.", "dishes": [{"name": "Anchovy fillets in olive oil", "note": "Salt-cured and hand-filleted; the house product", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Whole salted anchovies", "note": "For the galley: rinse, fillet and dress", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Seitons (boquerones)", "note": "Fresh anchovies in vinegar; praised in an April 2026 review", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Museum ticket with tasting", "note": "Audio-guided visit ending on the Solés terrace; about EUR 6-8", "kind": "dish"}], "caveat": "Hours come from a third-party ticket site only. Under-10s must be with an adult in the museum.", "neighborhood": "L'Escala · Closa d'en Llop", "signal_chip": {"label": "Since 1888", "full": "Solés salting house since 1888 · factory-museum opened for the 130th anniversary", "cosign": "the anchovy to carry home"}, "category": "larder", "hot_this_month": "The anchovy festa is over (4 Oct 2026), but the salt-cured filets are sold all year: stock the galley here (checked 19 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v11-mercat-del-lle", "cat": "market", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 11, "badge": "MARKET", "name": "Mercat del Lleó", "short": "Mercat del Lleó", "lat": 41.97915, "lng": 2.82255, "tags": ["Girona · Eixample, by the Onyar", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Market", "Produce", "Fish"], "why": "The Mercat del Lleó opened on 3 November 1944, in a building whose architects were chosen by the Franco regime after the Civil War, and it is still the city's main covered food market. Stallholders start early: a 2008 report noted many of them begin winding down well before lunchtime, which is why a Friday-afternoon opening was debated then. Inside are Girona's butchers, fishmongers, cheese and charcuterie counters, and in autumn the wild mushrooms.", "address": "Plaça de Francesc Calvet i Rubalcaba, 17002 Girona", "phone": "", "hours": "Year-round, Monday to Saturday; closed Sunday · Call ahead: an undated expat guide says Mon-Sat 7am-2pm plus Friday 5pm-8pm; a 2008 Nació Digital report gave Mon-Sat 8am-1.45pm; the old record said arrive before 1.30pm", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercat+del+Lleó+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "Market prices", "reservation": "Walk-in", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "Girona's municipal food hall, opened in November 1944, where the stalls trade from early morning.", "verdict": "Go in the morning, before the counters thin out, and shop for the galley or a picnic: botifarra, Empordà cheese, autumn bolets. Pair it with coffee in the Old Town across the river.", "dishes": [{"name": "Bolets", "note": "Wild mushrooms in season, October and November", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Embotits", "note": "Botifarra and fuet from the charcuterie counters", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Empordà cheeses", "note": "Local cheeses at the dairy stalls", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Fish from the coast", "note": "Roses and Palamós fish at the fishmongers", "kind": "dish"}], "caveat": "No 2026-dated source found; hours differ between sources, so assume mornings only and treat Friday afternoon as unconfirmed. Not to be confused with the Mercat de la Lleona, the Saturday flea market.", "neighborhood": "Girona · Eixample, by the Onyar", "signal_chip": {"label": "Since 1944", "full": "Municipal covered market, opened 3 November 1944", "cosign": "where Girona shops for the kitchen"}, "category": "larder", "hot_this_month": "Autumn bolets on the stalls, and Girona's Fires de Sant Narcís run 23 Oct-1 Nov around the corner; it is the usual stage for the new-oil presentation in mid-December (checked 19 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v15-la-f-brica", "cat": "shop", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 15, "badge": "CAFE", "name": "La Fábrica", "short": "La Fábrica", "lat": 41.98393, "lng": 2.82595, "tags": ["Girona · Barri Vell", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Cafe"], "why": "Christian Meier, a Canadian professional cyclist, and his wife Amber opened La Fábrica in March 2015, soon after he had ridden the Tour de France, and at the time it was the only café in Girona roasting its own beans. The beans now come from their second shop, Espresso Mafia, where Christian roasts on a 15-kilo Joper. Old bicycles hang on the stone walls, and riders in kit fill the street terrace each morning.", "address": "Carrer de la Llebre 3, 17004 Girona", "phone": "", "hours": "Year-round; no 2026-dated evidence found · Call ahead: Time Out (undated) lists Mon-Sun 9am-3pm", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Fábrica+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "EUR 5-18 (seen Jun 2026); coffee about EUR 3-4 in an older review", "reservation": "Walk-in; expect a queue at weekends", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "The specialty coffee bar a Tour de France rider and his wife opened in 2015, bikes hung on the walls.", "verdict": "Coffee first: a flat white or filter, then a cinnamon bun if the queue allows. For crew on a rest day, or anyone curious about Girona's cycling life.", "dishes": [{"name": "Flat white", "note": "Espresso from beans roasted by Espresso Mafia", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Single-origin filter", "note": "Hand-brewed from the house roast", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Cinnamon bun", "note": "The signature pastry", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Fruit bowl", "note": "Fresh fruit for a lighter breakfast", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Burrata salad", "note": "One of the brunch plates", "kind": "dish"}], "caveat": "No 2026-dated review or post found, so trading now is likely but unconfirmed. Some reviewers find the food pricey or slow; the coffee is the reason to go.", "neighborhood": "Girona · Barri Vell", "signal_chip": {"label": "Since 2015", "full": "Opened March 2015 by Christian and Amber Meier · own roast via Espresso Mafia", "cosign": "where Girona's pro riders take coffee"}, "category": "bars"},
    {"id": "v16-rocambolesc", "cat": "shop", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 16, "badge": "GELATERIA", "name": "Rocambolesc", "short": "Rocambolesc", "lat": 41.98474, "lng": 2.82351, "tags": ["Girona · Santa Clara, by the Onyar", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Cafe"], "why": "Rocambolesc began as the dessert cart at El Celler de Can Roca, which Jordi Roca and Alejandra Rivas wanted to wheel out onto the streets of Girona; the shop opened on Carrer de Santa Clara in 2012. It has since grown a confectionery next door (2022) and the Bikineria, a toasted-sandwich counter on Carrer de les Hortes. Opinionated About Dining placed the gelateria 60th on its Cheap Eats in Europe list for 2025.", "address": "Carrer de Santa Clara 50, 17001 Girona", "hours": "Year-round; no 2026-dated evidence found · Call ahead: Time Out lists noon-8.30pm weekdays; Pearl and En Primeur Club list 10.30am to 11pm (11.30pm Fri-Sat); Foodle 11am-11pm", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rocambolesc+Costa+Brava", "price_range": "EUR 4-8 (seen Jun 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-19", "hook": "Jordi Roca's ice-cream shop, born from the dessert trolley at El Celler de Can Roca.", "verdict": "The walk-in way to taste the Roca brothers' kitchen. Order the panet, warm ice-cream brioche, or a soft-serve with toppings; queues build on summer evenings.", "dishes": [{"name": "Panet", "note": "Ice cream inside a brioche, toasted warm in a press", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Soft-serve with toppings", "note": "Choose from more than 30 toppings", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Seasonal ice creams", "note": "Rotating flavours from the Roca dessert kitchen", "kind": "sweet"}], "web": "https://www.rocambolesc.com", "caveat": "Hours differ between listings (noon to 20:30 on weekdays in one, 10:30 to 23:00 in others), and one listing gives Carrer de les Hortes 6 instead of Santa Clara 50: check before you walk over. Nothing dated 2026 was found, and nothing says it closed.", "neighborhood": "Girona · Santa Clara, by the Onyar", "signal_chip": {"label": "OAD 2025", "full": "Opinionated About Dining Cheap Eats Europe: No. 43 (2023), No. 34 (2024), No. 60 (2025)", "cosign": "the Roca dessert trolley, walk-in"}, "category": "bars"}
